= Attention — Simple =

'''Attention''' is how the mind gives priority to some information instead of treating everything equally.

You might focus on one voice in a noisy room, look for a red car in traffic, or keep a problem in mind while ignoring distractions.

Things can grab attention because they stand out. That is related to [[Salience/Simple|salience]].

But attention can also follow your goals. You can deliberately look for something that does not stand out at all.

Attention is not exactly the same as awareness, and it is not the same as simply looking at something.

